        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Podocarpus, Osmunda\n- Taxonomy: genus, species, Podocarpaceae\n\nFacts:\n- Podocarpus is a genus of conifers in the podocarp family Podocarpaceae.\n- Podocarpus is the most numerous and most widely distributed genus in the family Podocarpaceae.\n- Podocarpus plants are evergreen shrubs or trees that are usually 1 to tall and can reach 40 m.\n- Podocarpus includes approximately 97 to 107 species, depending on species circumscription.\n- Osmunda has had five to ten species listed for the genus.",
